3. Exploitation & Decryption Process
Decryption Logic
The encryption is an affine transformation:  

ct ≡ (123 ⋅ pt + 19) (mod 256)

Reversed algebraically:  

pt ≡ 179 ⋅ (ct - 19) (mod 256)  

(where 179 is the modular inverse of 123 modulo 256).

Python Decryption Script (Final Version)

ct_hex = "6e0a9372ec49a3f6930ed8723f9df6f6720ed8d89dc4937222ec7214d89d1e0e352ce0aa6ec82bf622227bb70e7fb7352249b7d893c493d8539dec8fb7935d490e7f9d22ec89b7a322ec8fd80e7f8921"

ct = bytes.fromhex(ct_hex)

  

pt = []

for c in ct:

    pt_byte = (179 * (c - 19)) % 256

    pt.append(pt_byte)

  

plaintext = bytes(pt).decode('ascii')

print(plaintext)

